Scholarship and financial aid policy (plain-text source fixture)

The university scholarship policy describes eligibility, application, renewal, and review. Applicants submit the form and supporting evidence before the published deadline. Awards are based on the criteria announced for the relevant academic year. A recipient must remain enrolled, satisfy the required academic progress, and notify the university of a material change in circumstances. Renewal is not automatic and may depend on available funds. The committee records decisions and provides an appeal route for an incomplete or incorrect assessment.
Financial aid is credited to the student account after verification. The student remains responsible for charges not covered by the award. False information may lead to cancellation and recovery of funds. The policy is administered by student services and is reviewed at the end of each academic year so that criteria and deadlines remain clear to applicants.
Operational guidance: applicants should use the current form, submit complete evidence, and read the call carefully. The committee may request clarification before deciding. Appeals identify the decision, explain the alleged error, and include evidence. Recipients report changes in enrollment and circumstances promptly. Award notices state value, duration, conditions, and acceptance steps. Records are retained under the university records schedule.
